WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Start with a simple French sentence:

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.980
«Je regarde le film».

3
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.420
In English, swap the film for
'it' and nothing else moves.

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.710
I watch the film.

5
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.940
I watch it.

6
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.330
But a French speaker says,

7
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.480
word for word, 'I it watch'.

8
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.670
French uses two tiny words here:

9
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.910
«le» and «la».

10
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.300
And 'her' behaves just
as strangely as 'it'.

11
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.570
So where exactly do these little
words for 'it' and 'her' go,

12
00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.980
every time? In this mission,

13
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.280
you'll watch a chip jump,

14
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.260
then sort pronouns into two columns.

15
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.690
Then you'll see what happens
with 'not' and with two verbs,

16
00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.380
and place pronouns yourself in the lab.

17
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: find out
where the little words go.
